%% alt: Five steps, top to bottom. One, expand: add the display_name column and deploy code that writes both columns. Two, backfill: copy fullname into display_name for old rows. Three, switch reads to display_name once the copy is verified. Four, contract: stop writing fullname. Five, drop the fullname column. Every step before the drop can be rolled back.
%% caption: Every step works with both the old and the new code, so you can pause or roll back at any point before the final drop.
flowchart TB
  e["1 · Expand<br/>add display_name;<br/>write both columns"]
  b["2 · Backfill<br/>copy fullname<br/>into old rows"]
  r["3 · Switch reads<br/>to display_name,<br/>once verified"]
  c["4 · Contract<br/>stop writing<br/>fullname"]
  d["5 · Drop<br/>the fullname<br/>column"]
  e --> b --> r --> c --> d
